%% D2. Paired tests, repeated-measures ANOVA, LMM, GEE and GLMM
%% A guide to reasoning, not an automatic rule for choosing a model.
flowchart TD
  A["Two occasions only, complete pairs, a within-group question?"] -->|Yes| P["Paired t-test; for group comparisons, ANCOVA on follow-up (Module 3)"]
  A -->|No| B["Fixed occasions shared by all, complete data, continuous outcome?"]
  B -->|"Yes, and a descriptive test of time is enough"| R["Repeated-measures ANOVA with Greenhouse-Geisser or Huynh-Feldt correction (Module 3)"]
  B -->|"No: missed visits, dropout, irregular times, time-varying covariates"| C["Continuous outcome?"]
  R -.->|"An LMM answers the same question and more"| L
  C -->|Yes| L["Linear mixed model, or GLS with a chosen covariance (Modules 4-6)"]
  C -->|"No: binary, count"| D["Population-average or subject-specific target? (diagram D3)"]
  D -->|Population-average| G["GEE with robust SEs (Module 7); check the number of clusters and the missing-data assumption"]
  D -->|"Subject-specific, or MAR validity from likelihood needed"| M["GLMM (Module 8)"]
  L --> N["Then: missing data (D5) and diagnostics (D6)"]
  G --> N
  M --> N
  classDef q fill:#ffffff,stroke:#555555,color:#222222;
  classDef m fill:#eef4f8,stroke:#0b5d8f,color:#222222;
  class A,B,C,D,N q;
  class P,R,L,G,M m;
